WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:01.166
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.166 --> 00:00:03.490
- [Narrator] Democrats
led by President Biden say

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:06.190
now is the time to build back better.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:09.980
- The American Jobs Plan
will modernize 20,000 miles

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:14.360
on highways, roads, and main
street that are in difficult,

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.590
difficult shape right now.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:18.840
- [Narrator] But leaders don't
just want to build and update

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:23.000
roads, in some cases they
want highways torn down.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.100
Democrats would like to
provide funding to tear

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.150
down highways that had a damaging effect

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.600
on urban minority communities.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.120
- Federal funds created

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:35.370
the damage done here and
federal funds should be used

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:37.040
to help remedy it.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.890
- [Narrator] Activists in cities
like Tampa, Austin, Texas,

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:43.160
New Orleans, Detroit, and
Tulsa, Oklahoma are calling

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.830
for the removal of highways
that they say segregate

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:48.700
communities and harm minorities.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:51.460
Leaders say there are many
more examples like this road

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:52.623
in West Baltimore.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:56.700
This is the Franklin-Mulberry Expressway,

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.370
Baltimore locals call it
the highway to nowhere

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:01.723
and some policymakers
want to tear it down.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:05.320
The road cuts through
1.4 miles of the city

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:09.023
providing a speedy route for
cars traveling east to west.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.610
Like other parts of the
country's Interstate System,

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:15.500
the road was built to provide
fast access for traffic

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.890
from ports and downtown
offices to the suburbs,

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:21.730
but locals like Baltimore
City Councilman John Bullock

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:25.290
say it's a scar running
through the city's west side.

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:28.620
- The reality is that you
did have intact, businesses,

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.860
churches, families, community
networks that were literally

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:35.730
torn asunder with this
highway going through.

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.430
And yes, there are examples
of cities across the country

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:41.590
and Baltimore is no different
that during urban renewal

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:44.130
you saw the disproportionate
effects in neighborhoods

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:46.303
that had African-American populations.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:50.090
- [Narrator] Planning for this
road dates back to the 1950s

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:52.680
when President Eisenhower
called for cities to build

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.520
better connections to
the Interstate System.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:58.490
His goal was to give the
military, traders, and commuters

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:00.223
quick routes through the nation.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.960
In Baltimore the first round
of demolition displaced

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:05.570
hundreds of families,

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:08.170
that sparked a wave of
opposition from locals

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:11.570
like then City Councilwoman
Barbara Mikulski who would go on

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:14.580
to represent Maryland in
Congress as a Democrat.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.710
- [Barbara] New government
under eminent domain tucked

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:19.610
their house and cleared that
land without any relocation

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:23.900
benefits but they have a
fair market value in showing.

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:26.830
- [Narrator] Senator Chris
Van Hollen is Mikulski's

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:27.960
successor.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:32.960
- What you see here is a part
of the highway that was built

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:38.970
decades ago but was never
completed because Senator Mikulski

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:42.070
and other activists rallied to stop it,

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:44.550
and they were successful
at stopping the highway

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:48.810
but not before this one
and a half mile segment

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:53.420
had been built displacing over
900 people from their homes,

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:58.120
splitting an African American
community that had been stable

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:02.240
and vibrant and so here you see this scar.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:04.640
- [Narrator] Since then researchers
have found that highways

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:07.810
create challenging
conditions within cities.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:10.940
Data collected in Baltimore
suggests that air quality

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.600
is poorest and the sections
of the city that are near

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:14.843
Interstate connections.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:18.340
The Environmental Protection
Agency says that poor air

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:21.233
quality can worsen health
conditions like asthma.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:25.350
The Interstate also
contributed to out migration,

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:28.020
not only in Baltimore but
in cities across the country

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:28.853
like Detroit.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.830
Economists say that the highway
building in majority Black

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:36.750
Detroit contributed to the
city's economic decline.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.600
Maintenance costs for these
roads continue to weigh

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:42.933
on the city which filed
for bankruptcy in 2013.

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:46.540
This form of structural
inequity is what leaders

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:49.370
in Washington say they
are trying to address.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:51.830
- Too often investments have
failed to meet the needs

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.893
of marginalized communities left behind.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:57.440
- [Narrator] Developers today
say that tearing down parts

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:59.710
of the Interstate System
could correct a wave

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:01.670
of past failures.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:05.590
One 2018 review of West Baltimore
calls for the demolition

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:08.600
of two bridges at the
Eastern stub of the highway

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.300
opening more land for development.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.470
The plan says the new space could be used

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:17.633
for athletic fields, parks,
and a new retail center.

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:22.080
The panel also called for the
rehabilitation of vacant lots

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:25.943
in nearby row homes and wider
sidewalks for pedestrians.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:29.490
If Congress passes an infrastructure bill

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.130
the federal funding could help turn some

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:33.173
of these ideas into reality.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:37.250
West Baltimore Community
Organizer, Ashiah Parker

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.780
says she would welcome changes
in her part of the city

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:42.050
but she wants to make sure
the community has a seat

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:42.910
at the table.

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:46.120
- We definitely don't want
our federal partners putting

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:48.913
up large condos that people aren't able,

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:53.540
well that current residents
aren't able to occupy.

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:56.750
And then we also wanna make
sure that economic development

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:57.583
is done.

00:04:57.583 --> 00:05:00.940
So produce stores are other
types of small businesses

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:03.060
for people who are
already in a neighborhood

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:05.010
that can utilize.

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:06.950
- [Narrator] Other residents
said that they would like

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:09.880
for the government to focus
on rehabilitating homes

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:12.533
in the area before focusing on the roads.

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:16.590
The national movement to tear
down highways is picking up

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:19.820
steam as leaders in Congress
from both sides of the aisle

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:21.670
signal that they're open to the idea.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.260
The movement got a boost
from President Biden

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:29.000
when he called for $20 billion
to redress inequities created

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:32.070
by past investments in transportation.

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:35.090
That's just one part of the
bigger American Jobs Plan

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:38.033
which the White House says
would cost $1.7 trillion.

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:41.900
Senate Republicans now
say that they are open

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:44.563
to a nearly $1 trillion
infrastructure plan.

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:48.320
In short, both parties want to invest more

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:51.070
in infrastructure but they're
far apart on the details

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:53.120
of how it should be done.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:56.080
Republican senators say they're
open to using federal funds

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:59.230
to remove highways but they
want to leave the decision

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:01.000
to state lawmakers.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:04.000
- There are multiple examples
of poor planning decisions

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.550
that have led to adverse
consequences for specific

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:07.390
communities.

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:09.910
None of us denying that
and I think we all agree

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:11.870
they should be rectified.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:13.350
I believe it should be done at the local

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:15.670
and state level where
decision-makers are closest

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:19.060
to the people and able to
make a balanced decision.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:21.220
- [Narrator] The call to
fund highway removal breaks

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:24.330
from years of American
transportation philosophy.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:27.480
If a bill materializes highway
tear downs could unfold

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:29.113
in cities across the country.

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:34.477
(upbeat music)

